      "body": "## Summary\n\n```text\nAppTests/ActiveTimeWait.swift        wait loop: off-main heartbeat; a main-loop gap is discounted only if the heartbeat was silent too; order: wall cap, charged budget, then the condition\nAppTests/Issue507AliasFolderScanTests.swift   issue507FolderPathsComplete / Delivered507Rig.within2s use it; failure prints lifecycle + scanner + access log on one clock\nApp/Access/FolderOpenLifecycle.swift (new)    internal trace of one folder open: start, handoff, completed, rejected (reason), cancelled, thrown; exactly one terminal event per task\nApp/CanvasWindowController.swift              hooks in openGrantedFolder/openFolder (internal observer, nil in production; no path in any .public log)\nAppTests/Issue600{Heartbeat,Lifecycle,ScanWait}Tests.swift   gate/clock tests\n```\n\n#600: `issue507FolderPathsComplete` failed on CI five times with the same shape (scan nil or still scanning at the 2 s wall deadline): runs 42369028897, 42728233488, 43163508262, 44714991399 (PR #796) and 44724755518 (main). The traces show the grant and openFolder had finished and then nothing ran on the main actor for seconds; when it resumed, the deadline had expired before the open's remaining turns. The cause of the hosted stalls is not attributed. This change makes the wait charge only time the process was running, charges main-only gaps as product latency, and prints the open's lifecycle so the next failure explains itself. All assertions of issue507 are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- RED receipts I600-WI-1R (superseded), I600-F1-WI-1, I600-F1-WI-2, I600-F2-WI-1/2, all SEPARATION-HELD at record time (I600-F1-WI-1 no longer matches its file after a later line change; stated in the handoff).\n- Forced ordering: an injected clock stalls 2.5 s; the wall-clock wait fails with the CI signature, the new wait passes; a main-only gap with the heartbeat ticking is charged; a condition that first holds after 2 s of charged time fails.\n- Gates on 1323ca07 (third run; two earlier runs failed only a node test outside the diff under XProtect load): swift 2436, lcov exact 100% (17375/17375 lines, 4074/4074 functions), xcodegen/xcodebuild 0, retained App group 711/0, Node 1673 pass 0 fail 3 skipped, ledger/diffcheck/design 0, focused issue507|issue600 29/29, repeated 10x 10/10, test declarations 4438 to 4457.\n- Rebased onto 468f6bb6: rebase-verify CODE same ea60f32c755f23623b661d344788361dc02a0791.\n- mado-verify: https://github.com/anzchy/mado/issues/600#issuecomment-7042240544 (covers 1323ca07, the pre-rebase head).\n\n## UI-Parity\n\n| State | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Opening a folder through a symlink/alias path: scan completes, title, recents, grid search available | AUTO-PASS | App tests issue507FolderPathsComplete (both scanners), Issue600 tests |\n| Production behaviour with the lifecycle observer nil is unchanged | AUTO-PASS | retained App group 711/0; seam is internal and nil unless a test sets it |\n| The same flows on a real desktop | NOT VERIFIED | no device run in this PR; App tests only |\n\n## Review\n\n| Round | Range | gpt-auditor | opus-auditor |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| blind audit (Medium) | 957391d7..d65bef21 | 2 High (wait can pass a slow product step; lifecycle/cancellation diagnosis absent), 1 Medium | 0 High, 3 Medium, 3 Low |\n| confirm round 2 | d65bef21..4a8997db | 1 High left (condition true on an over-budget look still passed), 1 Medium, 1 Low | 0 High, 1 Medium, 2 Low |\n| fix round 2 (owner decision: fix once more, small) | 4a8997db..1323ca07 | not re-audited | not re-audited |\n\n### Still open\n- The gpt High from round 2 (success before the budget check) was fixed in 1323ca07 and the two Mediums/Lows with it, but the fix round was not re-audited (owner decision).\n- The hosted stalls are not explained; close #600 only after hosted runs show `stalls=[...]` (process-wide) or `charged=[...]` (main busy) in the [i507] line.\n- A process-wide stall longer than the cap minus 2 s still fails (34 s for FolderPathsComplete, 18 s with the 20 s default); the longest recorded is 16.4 s.\n- The Delivered507 rig's worst case is 160 s of its 180 s limit.\n- operation-superseded is not instrumented as a distinct reason.\n- Local Node flake candidates under XProtect load (not in this diff): scripts/perf/p308.test.mjs \"launch: a child that exits during start-up\", i632M1.\n\n## Gates\n\n| Lane | Status | SHA | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| package-tests | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | swift 2436 tests, measured on 1323ca07 before the rebase onto 468f6bb6 (rebase-verify CODE same ea60f32c755f23623b661d344788361dc02a0791) |\n| package-coverage | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | Package lines 17375/17375, functions 4074/4074, measured on 1323ca07 (CODE same) |\n| app-tests | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | retained App group 711/0 measured on 1323ca07 (CODE same); hosted group skipped locally, hosted CI binding |\n| unsigned-build | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | xcodebuild 0 measured on 1323ca07 (CODE same) |\n| node-tooling | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | node 1673 pass 0 fail 3 skipped measured on 1323ca07 (CODE same) |\n| ledger | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | ledger 0 |\n| diff-check | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | git diff --check 0 |\n| design-check | N/A | — | no design change |\n| audit | PASS | baf1eae59309c47c0a185585ffcf9a238f148bbf | two audit rounds on d65bef21 and 4a8997db; no Critical open; the remaining High was fixed by owner decision in 1323ca07 without re-audit (see Review) |\n| device-smoke | N/A | — | App-test-covered; no real-desktop run |\n\nDevice-Smoke: n/a — App-test-covered folder-open wait and trace, no real-desktop run\n\nLedger-Gardener: DAILY 468f6bb..baf1eae (covered by the daily sweep)\n\nRefs #600 #658 #620\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"
